    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Ali returns six months after his first visit. He continues carbidopa-levodopa one and a half tablets three times a day before meals, with phone alarms, and has noticed no wearing-off, involuntary movements, or lightheadedness. He finished physical therapy and keeps up about 180 minutes a week of walking, stationary cycling, and balance exercises. He practices his voice exercises daily. He has had no falls. When asked about impulse control today, he reports no new urges to gamble, shop, or eat and no compulsive hobbies. He has not yet seen a dentist. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Levodopa 150 mg three times daily before meals; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Motor complications</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Exercise</td><td>About 180 minutes a week</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None in six months</td></tr><tr><td>Impulse control</td><td>No new urges or compulsive behaviors</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

