    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Parkinson&apos;s disease, Hoehn and Yahr stage 2.5 (G20.A1)</content>. Stable: MDS-UPDRS Part III 24, no motor complications, no orthostatic hypotension, and no falls in six months. Impulse-control screen negative. [S]<list><item>Continue carbidopa-levodopa 150 mg three times daily before meals.</item><item>Continue exercise at 150 minutes a week or more.</item><item>Dental examination to be arranged at the preventive visit.</item><item>Yearly movement disorders review in the spring, with the genetic testing decision.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Hypokinetic dysarthria with soft speech (R47.1)</content>. Gains from speech therapy maintained. [S]<list><item>Continue daily voice exercises.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>MDS-UPDRS Parts III and IV and Hoehn and Yahr stage</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Part III 24, unchanged; Hoehn and Yahr 2.5; Part IV: no motor complications</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Orthostatic blood pressure, supine and after 3 minutes standing</td><td>Every visit while on dopaminergic treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>128/80 mmHg supine and 120/78 mmHg at 3 minutes standing; no orthostatic hypotension</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Dopaminergic regimen review for wearing-off, dyskinesia, and on-off</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No wearing-off or dyskinesia; no change</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Avoidance of dopamine-blocking drugs</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No dopamine-blocking drugs</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Medication side effects and adherence</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No side effects or missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall query and fall-risk assessment (Timed Up and Go, pull test)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls in six months; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Psychotic symptoms (hallucinations, delusions)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Impulse-control screen (QUIP-RS)</td><td>Every visit; mandatory on a dopamine agonist</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Negative; the screen missed at three months was done today</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Exercise counseling: aerobic, resistance, and balance, at least 150 minutes a week</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About 180 minutes a week</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning and goals of care</td><td>At diagnosis and at least yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>At the preventive visit next month</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Diagnosis review against the MDS clinical diagnostic criteria</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Confirmed by neurology six months ago; next review in the spring</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (MoCA)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 27 of 30 seven months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Depression, anxiety, and apathy (PHQ-9)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-9 3 seven months ago; mood good today; depression screen at the preventive visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Sleep: REM sleep behavior disorder questionnaire, Epworth Sleepiness Scale, insomnia, restless legs</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No dream enactment or daytime sleepiness</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Autonomic symptoms: constipation, urinary, sexual, sweating, drooling</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No autonomic symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Swallowing screen (EAT-10)</td><td>At least yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No choking or coughing with meals; EAT-10 due at the first visit next year</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Speech and voice loudness</td><td>Yearly; speech therapy for speech change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Gains maintained with daily practice</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Physical, occupational, and speech therapy</td><td>At diagnosis, then reassessed yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Physical therapy and speech therapy completed; reassess yearly</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Genetic testing with counseling</td><td>Once, offered to every person with Parkinson&apos;s disease</td><td>Due</td><td>Decision at the yearly neurology review</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Dental and oral examination</td><td>Every 6 months</td><td>Deferred</td><td>No dental examination in the six months since the first visit, a deviation from the protocol. He has no drooling, mouth pain, or chewing problems, so no harm is evident. Corrective action: a dental appointment is to be arranged at the preventive visit next month</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Driving safety</td><td>Yearly or with a motor or cognitive change</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No change; review at the first visit next year</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccination status (influenza, pneumococcal, zoster, COVID-19, Tdap)</td><td>Yearly, per the CDC schedule</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza, pneumococcal, and zoster vaccines at the preventive visit next month</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>Routine laboratory monitoring</td><td>Not required for Parkinson&apos;s disease surveillance</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>The CMID monograph calls for no routine laboratory tests; baseline blood count, chemistry, vitamin B12, and TSH were normal at the first visit</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Brain MRI</td><td>If atypical parkinsonism features appear</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No atypical features; examination stable</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Polysomnography for REM sleep behavior disorder</td><td>If REM sleep behavior disorder treatment is considered</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No dream enactment</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>AGS Beers Criteria medication review</td><td>Yearly from age 65</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>He is 54</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Deep brain stimulation programming review</td><td>Every 6 to 12 months after implantation</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No deep brain stimulator</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Less slowness of movement after a levodopa adjustment, without dyskinesia or orthostatic hypotension, by the three-month review. Outcome by 2026-06-09: MDS-UPDRS Part III fell from 30 to 24; no dyskinesia; no orthostatic hypotension [S]</item><item>Complete a four-week intensive speech therapy course and keep up daily voice practice. Outcome by 2026-06-09: LSVT LOUD course completed; easier to hear in conversation; daily home practice continues [S]</item><item>No falls through the six-month review, with at least 150 minutes a week of exercise including balance work. Outcome by 2026-09-08: No falls; Timed Up and Go improved from 13 to 11 seconds; exercising about 180 minutes a week [S]</item><item>Name a health care agent and record his goals of care by the preventive visit. In progress; target 2026-10-06 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Dopaminergic Therapy for Motor Symptoms in Early Parkinson Disease Practice Guideline Summary: A Report of the AAN Guideline Subcommittee (2021); MDS clinical diagnostic criteria for Parkinson&apos;s disease (2015); The recommendations of a consensus panel for the screening, diagnosis, and treatment of neurogenic orthostatic hypotension and associated supine hypertension (2017); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, Parkinson&apos;s disease monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Periodic preventive visit in four weeks, with vaccines, advance care planning, and the dental appointment. Quarterly Parkinson&apos;s disease review in three months. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-06: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

